    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1498">

                <pb facs="1616" n="1602" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1602"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.24/8–144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-01T18:00:00-03:00">August 1, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 1—5:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>739. PC<anchor n="37" xml:id="d1498-f1"/> boat furnished Uruguay under lend-lease
                    arrived Montevideo yesterday after uneventful trip. Naval Attaché states
                    President going aboard this afternoon, Uruguayan authorities very pleased, and
                    officers and crew of vessel delighted with training and treatment in United
                    States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1498-f1" n="37" xml:id="d1498-f1-content">
                <p>Patrol vessel, submarine chaser.</p>
